.cbx-sal-res .sal-tbl td,.cbx-sal-res .sal-tbl th{padding:.5rem .45rem}
.cbx-sal-res .sal-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1rem}
.cbx-sal-res .sal-taxable{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 .6rem}
@media(max-width:640px){.cbx-sal-res .sal-leg{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
@media(max-width:480px){.cbx-sal-res .sal-tbl{font-size:.82rem}.cbx-sal-res .sal-leg{grid-template-columns:1fr}.cbx-sal-res .cbx-panel{padding:1rem .8rem}}
</style><div class="cbx-panel"><h4>Where your gross salary goes</h4>##gross_bar##</div><div class="cbx-panel"><h4>Income tax, band by band</h4><p class="sal-taxable">Taxable income <b>&euro;##taxable_f##</b> = gross salary &minus; pension relief &minus; personal allowance (&euro;##allow_f## for ##status_f##). Each band taxes only the slice of income that falls inside it.</p>##band_table##</div>
<p class="cbx-note">Illustrative model: a generic five-band tax system with made-up allowances and rates, not any country&rsquo;s real rules. Effective rate = (income tax + social contributions) / gross. Marginal rate = income-tax band + social contributions + loan on your next euro. Not tax advice.</p>
</div>]]></exitlayout>
